          %blockquote
            %p Somebody should produce pictures like this here…
            %blockquote
              %p Well, it worked in the preview; a little help?
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            be a 1-dimensional manifold of the form of the interval
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/framing"} framing
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            is a trivialization of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi γ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\gamma \oplus \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1\} \subset \mathbb{R}
            be the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            as equipped with its canonical 2-framing, then a 2-framing of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            is induced by embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            into the plane and shading one of its two sides. This identifies at each point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in \gamma
            the tangent space to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            at that point with the tangent vector to the embedding of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            as a vector in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            and identifies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\in \mathbb{R}
            with the vector in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^2
            orthogonal to this tangent vector and pointing into the shaded region.
          %p
            This shows that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gamma
            is regarded with its two endpoints both as incoming or both as outgoing, then the induced 2-framing of these endpoints is opposite to each other. This way such an arc is a morphism from the union of the “positive point” and the “negative point” to the empty 0-manifold, hence is a unit/counit exhibiting these as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+objects"} dual objects
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#general General
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Bord
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_n
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category+with+all+adjoints"} (∞,n)-category with all adjoints
          %p
          #SymmetricMonoidalFunctorToCoSpans.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2Cn%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-functor"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                \-functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Bord
                      %mi n
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi CoSpan
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≡
                    %msub
                      %mi Corr
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Grpd
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Bord_n
                    \\longrightarrow
                    CoSpan_n(Grpd_\infty)
                    \\equiv
                    Corr_n\big(
                    Grpd_\infty^{op}
                    \\big)
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  from the unoriented
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-category+of+cobordisms"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                    \-category of cobordisms
              %li
                %p
                  to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-category"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                    \-category
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospans"} cospans
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoids"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                      \-groupoids
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2Cn%29-category+of+correspondences"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
                    \-category of correspondences
                  in the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} opposite
                  of
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Grpd"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi Grpd
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grpd_\infty
            %p given by
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  first regarding a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"} cobordism
                  as the higher
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cospan"} cospan
                  (in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmthMfd"} SmthMfd
                  = succeed "-inclusions" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
              %li
                %p
                  then applying the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shape+modality"} shape modality
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ʃ
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %mi SmthMfd
                          %mo ⟶
                          %msub
                            %mi Grpd
                            %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \esh \colon SmthMfd \longrightarrow Grpd_\infty
                  = succeed "/" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+infinity-groupoids"}
                      fundamental
                      = succeed "-groupoids" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mn ∞
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+types"} homotopy types
            %p
          The basic idea of this construction is common, but an actual proof of its symmetric monoidal
          = succeed "-functoriality" do
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#CalaqueHaugsengScheimbauer2025"} Calaque, Haugseng &amp; Scheimbauer 2025 Thm. D
          %h3#relation_to_thom_spectrum Relation to Thom spectrum
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \to \infty
            we have that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_{(\infty,\infty)}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite+loop+space"} infinite loop space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi M
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\infty M O
            that underlies the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
          %p
            Its
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+group"} homotopy group
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi n
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\pi_n Bord_{(\infty,\infty)} \simeq \Omega_n
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore a symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Bord_{(\infty,\infty)} \to S
          %p
            to some symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism"}> cobordism
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+cobordism"} extended cobordism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+cobordisms"} category of cobordisms
            %li
              %p
                %strong (∞,n)-category of cobordisms
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general_2 General
          %p
            A specific realization of this idea in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2Cn%29-category"} (∞,n)-category
            modeled as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-fold+complete+Segal+space"} n-fold complete Segal space
            is in (definition 2.2.9, page 36)
          %ul
            %li#LurieQFT
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+Classification+of+Topological+Field+Theories"} On the Classification of Topological Field Theories
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %a{:href => "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Bo8GNfN-Xn4"} Video Stream
          %p
            In that article a proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+hypothesis"} cobordism hypothesis
            is indicated. A review is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julie+Bergner"}> Julie Bergner
              ,
              %em
                Models for
                = succeed "-Categories" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn ∞
                        %mo ,
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,n)
              , in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              (eds.)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
              Available
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1011.0110"} on the arxiv
          %p Other discussions of higher categories of cobordismsL
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marco+Grandis"}> Marco Grandis
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cospans+in+Algebraic+Topology"} Cospans in Algebraic Topology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eugenia+Cheng"} Eugenia Cheng
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nick+Gurski"} Nick Gurski
                %em
                  Toward an
                  = succeed "-category" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                , Theory and Applications of Categories 18 (2007), 274-302. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/volumes/18/10/18-10abs.html"}> tac
                )
          %p
            Discussion in the context of promoting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AKSZ+sigma-models"} AKSZ sigma-models
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+functorial+field+theories"} extended functorial field theories
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
          %ul
            %li#CalaqueHaugsengScheimbauer2025
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Damien+Calaque"}> Damien Calaque
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rune+Haugseng"} Rune Haugseng
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudia+Scheimbauer"} Claudia Scheimbauer
              = succeed "," do
                %em The AKSZ Construction in Derived Algebraic Geometry as an Extended Topological Field Theory
              %strong 308
              1555 (2025) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2108.02473"}> arXiv:2108.02473
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/memo/1555"} doi:10.1090/memo/1555
          %h3#in_dimension_2 In dimension 2
          %p
            A detailed construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28n%2Cr%29-category"} (2,2)-category
            of 2-dimensional cobordisms is
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"}> Chris Schommer-Pries
                ,
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category+of+2-dimensional+cobordisms"} 2-category of 2-dimensional cobordisms
            %li#SchommerPries13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Schommer-Pries"}> Chris Schommer-Pries
                ,
                %em Dualizability in Low-Dimensional Higher Category Theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1308.3574"}> arXiv:1308.3574
                )
          %p
            Discussion of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of complex cobordisms, aimed at formalizing chiral
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Henriques"}> André Henriques
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The complex cobordism 2-category
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://andreghenriques.com/ComplexCob2CatandCentralExt.mp4"} video
          %h3#in_dimension_3 In dimension 3
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Bartlett"}> Bruce Bartlett
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Douglas"} Christopher Douglas
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christopher+Schommer-Pries"} Christopher Schommer-Pries
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jamie+Vicary"} Jamie Vicary
              %em Extended 3-dimensional bordism as the theory of modular objects
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1411.0945"}> arXiv:1411.0945
              )
          %h3#in_dimension_
            In dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            For a discussion of the relation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Bord
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo ,
                      %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Bord_{(\infty,\infty)}
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thom+spectrum"} Thom spectrum
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+ring"} cobordism ring
            see also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Francis"}> John Francis
              ,
              %em Cobordisms
              (notes by
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Owen+Gwilliam"} Owen Gwilliam
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.northwestern.edu/~jnkf/classes/mflds/2cobordism.pdf"} pdf
